# Documentation governance

- Start at `docs/README.md` and follow ADR-0001.
- Maintain one canonical active document per topic.
- Add the required metadata block to first-party Markdown. Embedded
  `crates/*/.agents/**` skill documents and the GitHub PR form are exempt.
- Describe current mechanics in code/config/schema or reference docs, durable
  boundaries in architecture, rationale in ADRs, and operations in runbooks.
- Never edit an accepted ADR; supersede it with a new numbered ADR.
- Put active plans only at `docs/plans/active/<initiative>/README.md` and keep
  them outcome-focused. Archive chronology and evidence.
- Put temporary prompts and session handoffs in ignored `.handoff/`.
- Link component-local docs from their component index and the central index.
- Generate dependency/version inventory from manifests; never update its table
  by hand.
- Run `python3 scripts/check-documentation.py` and the inventory `--check`
  before handoff.
